vaft-matlab: macOS (Apple silicon) build fixes for IMAS-MATLAB
==============================================================

Applied by install/install_imas_matlab.sh to a *copy* of the IMAS-MATLAB
tree on macOS only. Linux builds use upstream unchanged.

What it changes (CMakeLists.txt, ids_validate.xsl):
  * build al-mex as a shared C library on macOS, as upstream already does on
    Windows, and stop CMake's FindMatlab from adding C++ MEX export maps
    (Matlab_HAS_CPP_API FALSE) that the C MEX runtime cannot resolve;
  * compile every MEX target with MATLAB_DEFAULT_RELEASE=R2017b, the
    separate-complex API IMAS-MATLAB is written against;
  * set @loader_path / ../lib / MATLAB bin rpaths so MEX files find libal
    and libal-mex without DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH (stripped by macOS SIP);
  * use -Wl,--as-needed only on Linux (Apple ld rejects it);
  * replace `uint` (glibc-only typedef) with `unsigned int`.

The installed bin/al_env.sh comes from IMAS-Core; see
install/imas-core/macos.patch.

Tested on IMAS-MATLAB f8208f6 (5.5.0-63) and applies to develop 40c61b2.

